                <p>Aspects and embodiments may provide systems and methods for verifying that a user e.g. in an authentication system is a three-dimensional person, based on captured images. The methods and systems may comprise: capturing at least one first image of the user taken with a camera located at a first distance from the user, the camera associated with a computing device; processing the at least one first image or a portion thereof to create first biometric data, capturing, at the second distance, at least one second image of the user taken with the camera associated with the computing device, such that the second distance is different from the first distance; processing the at least one second image, or a portion thereof, to create second biometric data, processing the first biometric data and the second biometric data to determine whether expected differences exist between the first biometric data and the second biometric data to indicate an expected type of distorting change in at least one image that is consistent with a real person being imaged and which is indicative of three-dimensionality; and determining the user is not three-dimensional when the first biometric data and the second biometric data do not have the expected differences indicating the user exhibits three-dimensionality.</p>
